  "observations": {
    "O-101": "CLOSED: native key-tracking flags restored.",
    "O-102": "CLOSED: fresh declared output inventory and separate development failures.",
    "O-103": "RECORDED: the post-call TCR/getter comparison is a bound check, not an independent count witness. RM4 validation bound duplicates the getter bound. RM5 publication check is redundant with the admitted incrementing collector; RM1 demonstrates its value against a faulty collector. These clause omissions are equivalent under the admitted collector contract; keep defensive checks.",
    "O-104": "OPEN: saved-image count rebasing is not admitted. Add a restored-image collect-then-GETHASH witness when GC-lock functions land; current differing stamps conservatively request rehash.",
    "O-105": "OPEN: carry O-99 host immediate target encoding/refusal and O-100 descriptor refill, seek, %FASLOAD buffer, char-code-limit controls to target LOAD.",
    "O-97": "CLOSED: real successful-copy counter and original hash stamps.",
    "O-98": "CLOSED: directed admission controls; implied individual bounds recorded in loader-gc README."
  },
